insert into nodes (node_type, slug, title, summary, status, meta_title, meta_description, legacy_slugs, published_at) values ('article', 'maldives-in-november-weather-activities-expert-travel-guide', 'Maldives in November: Weather, Activities & Expert Travel Guide', 'Planning a trip to Maldives in November? Discover weather patterns, activities, prices, and expert tips for visiting during the start of the dry season. Find the best resorts and experiences for a November vacation.', 'published', 'Maldives in November: Weather, Activities & Expert Travel Guide | Maldives Travel Guide | MTG', 'Planning a trip to Maldives in November? Discover weather patterns, activities, prices, and expert tips for visiting during the start of the dry season. Find the best resorts and experiences for a November vacation.', ARRAY['/articles/maldives-in-november.html']::text[], now()) on conflict (node_type, slug) do nothing;
insert into articles (id, body, reading_time_minutes) select id, '<figure><img src="legacy/images/resorts/over-water-room-maldives-w.webp" alt="Maldives in November - water villa during early dry season" loading="lazy" /></figure><p>November in the Maldives marks the beginning of the dry season with excellent weather and pre-peak season value</p><p>November marks the beginning of the dry season in the Maldives, as the northeast monsoon (Iruvai) takes hold, bringing significantly improved weather conditions. With decreasing rainfall, lower humidity, calmer seas, and excellent underwater visibility, November offers an ideal combination of favorable weather and pre-peak season value. As tourist numbers begin to increase but remain below high season levels, November represents one of the best value-for-money periods to experience the Maldives at its near-best.</p><h4>November in the Maldives at a Glance</h4><ul><li>Weather: Beginning of dry season with decreasing rainfall and humidity</li><li>Tourist Traffic: Moderate (beginning to increase for high season)</li><li>Pricing: 15-30% lower than peak season rates</li><li>Water Visibility: Excellent (20-30 meters)</li><li>Marine Life: Abundant with excellent visibility for spotting various species</li><li>Surf Conditions: Decreasing swells as northeast monsoon establishes</li><li>Special Events: Republic Day celebrations (November 11th)</li></ul><div data-youtube-id="kSmRO7irtTA" data-video-title="Maldives in November - What to Expect"></div><p>Video: Experience the Maldives during the early dry season in November</p><h2>November Weather in the Maldives</h2><p>November marks the transition to the northeast monsoon (Iruvai) in the Maldives, bringing significantly improved weather conditions compared to the previous months. As the southwest monsoon retreats, rainfall decreases substantially, humidity levels drop, and periods of sunshine become longer and more consistent. While occasional brief showers may still occur, they typically pass quickly, giving way to clear blue skies and excellent visibility.</p><h3>Temperature &amp; Humidity</h3><p>November temperatures remain consistently warm and tropical, similar to other months in the Maldives. The key difference is the decreasing humidity levels as the dry season begins, making outdoor activities more comfortable. The warm ocean temperature ensures pleasant swimming and water activities throughout the month.</p><h3>Rainfall &amp; Wind</h3><p>November sees a significant decrease in rainfall compared to the previous months. When rain does occur, it''s typically in the form of brief showers rather than prolonged downpours. The northeast monsoon brings calmer seas and more predictable weather patterns, with increasing sunshine hours as the month progresses. The northern atolls generally experience the dry season conditions earlier than the southern atolls.</p><h3>Typical November Rain Pattern</h3><p>November rainfall in the Maldives typically follows a pattern of occasional brief showers with extended periods of sunshine. Here''s a visualization of how rain might distribute across a typical week in November:</p><p>This pattern is representative of typical November conditions, with predominantly sunny days and occasional brief showers.</p><h4>Regional Weather Variations</h4><p>While the Maldives has relatively consistent weather throughout its atolls, some regional variations can occur in November:</p><ul><li>Northern Atolls: Typically experience dry season conditions earlier, with less rainfall and more consistent sunshine.</li><li>Central Atolls: Generally follow the average November pattern with a mix of sunshine and occasional brief showers.</li><li>Southern Atolls: May experience slightly more rainfall as the transition to the dry season occurs later than in the northern regions.</li></ul><p>These variations are relatively minor, and November generally brings favorable weather conditions throughout the Maldives. For more information about different regions, check our Maldives islands guide.</p><h2>How November Compares to October and December</h2><p>Understanding how November compares to the months immediately before and after can help you decide if it''s the right time for your Maldives vacation:</p><h3>October</h3><p>October is a transitional month with improving weather conditions but still some influence from the southwest monsoon. It offers excellent value with fewer tourists than November. For more details, check our guide on visiting the Maldives in October.</p><h3>November</h3><p>November marks the beginning of the dry season with significantly improved weather conditions. It offers an excellent balance of favorable weather and pre-peak season value. Tourist numbers begin to increase but remain below high season levels, creating a pleasant atmosphere without overcrowding.</p><h3>December</h3><p>December sees the dry season in full effect with excellent weather conditions. However, it also marks the beginning of the peak tourist season, with significantly higher prices, especially during the Christmas and New Year period. Resorts are often fully booked well in advance for the holiday season.</p><h4>November Weather Compared to Other Months</h4><p>Where November sits in the annual Maldives weather pattern:</p><p>November marks the beginning of the dry season in the Maldives. While not quite as dry as January and February (the peak of the dry season), November offers significantly improved weather conditions compared to the wet season months. Rainfall decreases substantially, and sunshine hours increase, creating excellent conditions for beach activities and water sports. For more information about weather patterns throughout the year, see our guide on the cheapest time to visit the Maldives.</p><h4>Special Events in November</h4><p>November includes some special events and celebrations in the Maldives:</p><ul><li>Republic Day (November 11): A national holiday celebrating the establishment of the Republic of Maldives in 1968. Festivities include parades, cultural performances, and various events in Male and on local islands.</li><li>Victory Day (November 3): Commemorates the foiling of the 1988 coup attempt. While not as widely celebrated as Republic Day, some events may be held in Male.</li><li>Resort Special Events: As the high season approaches, many resorts begin organizing special themed events, culinary experiences, and entertainment programs for guests.</li></ul><p>For more information about Maldivian culture and events, see our guide on Maldivian culture.</p><h4>November Value Alert</h4><p>November offers good value in the Maldives, with discounts of 15-30% compared to peak season rates. As the month progresses, prices gradually increase in anticipation of the high season. Early November typically offers better deals than late November, with some resorts maintaining shoulder season pricing until mid-month. While not as inexpensive as the wet season months, November provides an excellent balance of favorable weather conditions and reasonable pricing before the peak season surge in December.</p><h2>Best Activities in the Maldives in November</h2><p>November''s excellent weather conditions and improving water visibility make it an ideal time for a wide range of activities in the Maldives. Here are the top experiences to enjoy during your November visit:</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/snorkeling-in-maldives.webp" alt="Snorkeling in Maldives in November" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Snorkeling &amp; Diving</h3><p>November offers excellent conditions for snorkeling and diving in the Maldives. With water visibility reaching 20-30 meters, underwater enthusiasts can enjoy crystal-clear views of the vibrant coral reefs and abundant marine life. The calmer seas of the northeast monsoon make water entry and exit easier, especially for novice snorkelers.</p><p>The eastern sides of the atolls typically offer better visibility during this period as the northeast monsoon establishes. Many dive sites become more accessible as sea conditions improve, and the variety of marine life visible is exceptional. For more information about diving and snorkeling spots, see our Maldives snorkeling and diving guide.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/addu-manta-point.webp" alt="Diving with marine life in Maldives in November" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Marine Life Encounters</h3><p>November is an excellent month for marine life encounters in the Maldives. As the northeast monsoon establishes, plankton levels decrease, leading to improved visibility that makes spotting larger marine species easier. Manta rays can still be found at cleaning stations, particularly in the eastern sides of atolls, while whale sharks continue to be spotted in South Ari Atoll year-round.</p><p>The changing currents bring a diverse range of marine life to the reefs, including reef sharks, turtles, eagle rays, and a variety of colorful reef fish. The excellent visibility makes November ideal for underwater photography of marine life. For more information about marine life, see our Maldives diving spots guide.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/water-sports-maldives.webp" alt="Water sports in Maldives in November" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Water Sports</h3><p>November''s calmer seas and consistent winds make it an excellent time for various water sports in the Maldives. Activities like jet skiing, wakeboarding, water skiing, and parasailing benefit from the improved sea conditions. The northeast monsoon provides ideal conditions for windsurfing and kitesurfing on the eastern sides of the atolls.</p><p>With increasing sunshine hours and less rainfall, water sports activities are less likely to be interrupted by weather conditions. Many resorts offer special water sports packages during this period as the high season approaches. For more information about water sports options, see our guide on things to do in the Maldives.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-beaches.webp" alt="Beach relaxation in Maldives in November" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Beach Activities</h3><p>November''s excellent weather conditions create perfect opportunities for beach activities in the Maldives. With increasing sunshine hours and decreasing rainfall, beach days become more reliable and enjoyable. The soft white sands are ideal for sunbathing, beach volleyball, sandcastle building, and romantic beach walks.</p><p>Many resorts organize special beach activities during this period, including beach barbecues, movie nights under the stars, and beach yoga sessions. The comfortable temperatures and lower humidity make November ideal for extended periods on the beach without the discomfort of excessive heat or humidity. For more beach experiences, see our guide on best beaches in the Maldives.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/fishing/night-fishing-in-maldives.webp" alt="Fishing in Maldives in November" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Fishing</h3><p>November offers excellent fishing conditions in the Maldives as the northeast monsoon establishes. The calmer seas make fishing excursions more comfortable, and the changing currents attract a variety of fish species. Traditional Maldivian sunset fishing is particularly rewarding during this period, with good chances of catching snappers, groupers, and jacks.</p><p>Big game fishing enthusiasts can target species like tuna, wahoo, mahi-mahi, and sailfish, which are abundant in Maldivian waters during November. Many resorts offer the option to have your catch prepared for dinner, creating a truly memorable dining experience. For more information about fishing experiences, check our Maldives fishing guide.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-culture.webp" alt="Cultural experiences in Maldives in November" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Cultural Experiences</h3><p>November is an excellent time to explore the cultural side of the Maldives, with Republic Day celebrations on November 11th offering unique insights into Maldivian traditions and national pride. Local island visits become more comfortable with the improved weather conditions, allowing visitors to explore authentic Maldivian communities, markets, and historical sites.</p><p>Many resorts organize cultural demonstrations during this period, including traditional Bodu Beru performances, cooking classes featuring Maldivian cuisine, and craft workshops. The increasing tourist numbers create a vibrant atmosphere while still being manageable compared to the peak season. For more cultural insights, see our guide on Maldivian culture.</p><h2>Best Resorts to Visit in November</h2><h2>Top Recommended Resorts for November</h2><p>November offers excellent conditions throughout the Maldives, making it a great time to visit almost any resort. However, some properties stand out for their particular offerings during this early dry season period. Here are our top recommendations for November visits:</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/baros-island/images/baros-maldives.webp" alt="Baros Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Baros Maldives</h3><p>November Special: From $750 per night (20% off peak season rates)</p><p>Located in North Male Atoll, Baros offers exceptional value in November with its house reef being particularly spectacular during this period of excellent visibility. The resort''s proximity to numerous dive sites makes it ideal for underwater enthusiasts looking to take advantage of November''s clear waters.</p><ul><li>House Reef: One of the best house reefs in the Maldives, easily accessible for snorkeling</li><li>Marine Center: Expert marine biologists offering guided reef tours</li><li>Dining: Lighthouse Restaurant offers spectacular overwater dining</li><li>Location: Just 25 minutes by speedboat from Male International Airport</li></ul><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-resort.webp" alt="Constance Halaveli" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Constance Halaveli</h3><p>November Special: From $850 per night (25% off peak season rates)</p><p>Located in North Ari Atoll, Constance Halaveli offers excellent value in November before the peak season price increases. The resort''s position provides access to some of the best dive sites in the Maldives, which benefit from the excellent visibility of the early dry season.</p><ul><li>Diving: Access to over 20 world-class dive sites in Ari Atoll</li><li>Water Sports: Extensive water sports center with perfect November conditions</li><li>Spa: Award-winning overwater spa with treatment rooms facing east for sunrise views</li><li>Dining: Multiple restaurants with special November menus</li></ul><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/velassaru/images/velassaru-maldives.webp" alt="Velassaru Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Velassaru Maldives</h3><p>November Special: From $650 per night (30% off peak season rates)</p><p>Located in South Male Atoll, Velassaru offers excellent value in November with its contemporary design and extensive water sports facilities. The resort''s house reef is particularly vibrant during this period of excellent visibility, and its proximity to Male makes transfers reliable even during occasional weather changes.</p><ul><li>Water Sports: Extensive center with perfect November conditions</li><li>House Reef: Vibrant reef accessible directly from the beach</li><li>Dining: Five restaurants including the overwater Chill Bar</li><li>Location: Just 25 minutes by speedboat from Male International Airport</li></ul><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/lily-beach/images/lily-beach-resort-and-spa-maldives.webp" alt="Lily Beach Resort &amp; Spa" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Lily Beach Resort &amp; Spa</h3><p>November Special: From $950 per night (all-inclusive, 20% off peak rates)</p><p>Located in South Ari Atoll, Lily Beach offers excellent value with its premium all-inclusive package in November. The resort''s position provides access to whale shark spotting areas, which benefit from the excellent visibility of the early dry season. The all-inclusive concept is perfect for enjoying the resort''s facilities without worrying about additional costs.</p><ul><li>All-Inclusive: Premium all-inclusive package covering fine dining and premium drinks</li><li>Marine Life: Close to whale shark spotting areas in South Ari Atoll</li><li>House Reef: Excellent house reef with easy access from water villas</li><li>Family-Friendly: Excellent kids club and family activities</li></ul><h2>Getting Around in November</h2><figure><img src="legacy/images/ferry/anantara-dhigu-maldives-airport-transfers.webp" alt="Speedboat Transfer" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Speedboat Transfers</h3><p>Excellent conditions in November</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/transfers/maldives-seaplane-transfers.webp" alt="Seaplane Transfer" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Seaplane Transfers</h3><p>Very reliable in November</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maps/fari-island-transfer.webp" alt="Domestic Flight Transfer" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Domestic Flight Transfers</h3><p>Excellent reliability in November</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/traditional-maldivian-boat.webp" alt="Public Ferry" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Public Ferry Transfers</h3><p>Regular schedules with good reliability</p><h2>Pros and Cons of Visiting the Maldives in November</h2><h3>Pros of Visiting in November</h3><ul><li>Excellent Weather: Beginning of the dry season with decreasing rainfall and humidity</li><li>Pre-Peak Season Value: 15-30% lower prices than peak season with excellent conditions</li><li>Excellent Water Visibility: 20-30 meters visibility for diving and snorkeling</li><li>Moderate Crowds: Busy enough for atmosphere but not overcrowded like peak season</li><li>Reliable Transfers: Fewer weather-related delays for seaplanes and boat transfers</li><li>Republic Day Celebrations: Opportunity to experience Maldivian cultural events</li><li>Abundant Marine Life: Excellent visibility for spotting various marine species</li><li>Perfect Beach Conditions: Increasing sunshine hours ideal for beach activities</li><li>Good Availability: Easier to secure bookings than during peak season</li></ul><h3>Cons of Visiting in November</h3><ul><li>Increasing Prices: Higher rates than wet season months, especially late November</li><li>Growing Crowds: More tourists than during the wet season months</li><li>Advance Booking Needed: Popular resorts begin filling up for high season</li><li>Occasional Showers: While significantly reduced, brief rain showers still possible</li><li>Decreasing Manta Activity: Fewer manta ray aggregations compared to wet season</li><li>Reduced Surfing Conditions: Swells decrease as northeast monsoon establishes</li><li>Higher Demand for Activities: Popular excursions may require advance booking</li><li>Variable Transition: Early November may still show some wet season patterns</li></ul><h2>What to Pack for the Maldives in November</h2><p>November''s favorable weather conditions make packing relatively straightforward, but it''s still important to be prepared for the tropical climate and occasional brief showers. Here''s a comprehensive packing list specifically tailored for a November visit:</p><h3>Clothing</h3><ul><li>Lightweight, breathable clothing (natural fabrics like cotton and linen work well)</li><li>Multiple swimwear options for daily water activities</li><li>Rash guard or UV protection shirt for snorkeling and water activities</li><li>Light rain jacket or poncho (for occasional brief showers)</li><li>Comfortable sandals and water shoes</li><li>Light sweater or wrap for air-conditioned spaces</li><li>Casual resort wear for dinners (check your resort''s dress code)</li><li>Hat with wide brim for sun protection</li><li>Sunglasses with UV protection</li></ul><h3>Health &amp; Protection</h3><ul><li>High SPF sunscreen (reef-safe/mineral-based recommended)</li><li>After-sun cooling gel or aloe vera</li><li>Insect repellent (though mosquitoes are less prevalent in November)</li><li>Basic first aid kit with band-aids, antiseptic, and pain relievers</li><li>Motion sickness medication (for boat transfers)</li><li>Personal medications with prescriptions</li><li>Hand sanitizer and disinfectant wipes</li><li>Lip balm with SPF protection</li><li>Rehydration salts or electrolyte tablets (for hot days)</li></ul><h3>Equipment &amp; Electronics</h3><ul><li>Underwater camera or GoPro for excellent visibility conditions</li><li>Waterproof phone case or pouch</li><li>Dry bag for boat trips and excursions</li><li>Power bank for charging devices during excursions</li><li>Universal power adapter</li><li>E-reader or books for beach reading</li><li>Portable Bluetooth speaker for your villa</li><li>Snorkeling equipment (though most resorts provide this)</li><li>Binoculars for marine life spotting from your villa</li></ul><h4>November Packing Tip</h4><p>While November marks the beginning of the dry season, it''s still wise to pack a light rain jacket or poncho for occasional brief showers. The sun is particularly strong in the Maldives, so prioritize sun protection including high SPF sunscreen, hats, and UV-protective clothing. For more general packing advice, see our comprehensive Maldives travel guide.</p><h2>Essential Travel Tips for Visiting the Maldives in November</h2><h3>Timing Your Visit</h3><p>Consider visiting in early to mid-November for the best balance of favorable weather and pre-peak season pricing. As the month progresses, prices begin to increase in anticipation of the high season, particularly around the American Thanksgiving holiday period.</p><p>If you''re interested in experiencing Republic Day celebrations on November 11th, plan to be in Male or on a local island on this date. Many resorts also organize special events to mark this important national holiday.</p><h3>Resort Selection</h3><p>November is an excellent time to visit resorts known for their house reefs and marine life, as the excellent visibility maximizes underwater experiences. Consider resorts in Ari Atoll for whale shark encounters or North Male Atoll for easy access to numerous dive sites.</p><p>Book your preferred resort well in advance, especially for the latter part of November, as properties begin filling up for the approaching high season. Many resorts offer early booking discounts that can provide significant savings.</p><h3>Transfer Considerations</h3><p>November offers reliable transfer conditions with the northeast monsoon establishing calmer seas and clearer skies. Seaplane transfers are particularly scenic during this period with excellent visibility and fewer weather-related delays.</p><p>If you''re planning to visit multiple resorts or islands, November''s favorable weather makes island hopping more reliable and enjoyable. For more information about transfers, see our Maldives transportation guide.</p><h3>Maximizing Value</h3><p>Look for early booking offers and shoulder season promotions, particularly for stays in early November. Many resorts maintain shoulder season pricing until mid-month, offering excellent value for the favorable weather conditions.</p><p>Consider booking half-board or full-board meal plans rather than all-inclusive packages in November. With excellent weather conditions, you''re likely to spend more time enjoying activities and excursions rather than resort-based food and beverages. For more tips on finding the best deals, see our guide on the cheapest time to visit the Maldives.</p><h3>Activity Planning</h3><p>Take advantage of November''s excellent visibility by prioritizing snorkeling, diving, and underwater photography. Book specialized marine excursions in advance, as these become increasingly popular as the high season approaches.</p><p>Consider booking sunset cruises and dolphin watching excursions, which benefit from the calmer seas and clearer skies of November. The changing light conditions during this transitional month can create spectacular sunset views.</p><h3>Photography Tips</h3><p>November''s excellent visibility and clear skies create ideal conditions for both underwater and landscape photography. The water clarity allows for exceptional underwater shots, while the dramatic cloud formations of the early dry season create spectacular sunset images.</p><p>If you''re visiting around Republic Day (November 11th), look for opportunities to photograph cultural celebrations and events, which offer unique insights into Maldivian traditions. For professional assistance, consider booking a private photographer during your stay.</p><h2>Recommended November Activities</h2><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/snorkeling-in-maldives.webp" alt="Snorkeling Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Snorkeling Tour</h3><p>Excellent visibility in NovemberDuration: 2-3hrs</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/maldives-diving-faru-reef.webp" alt="Diving Excursion" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Diving Excursion</h3><p>Crystal clear waters in NovemberDuration: 3-4hrs</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/dolphin-watching-tour.webp" alt="Dolphin Cruise" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Dolphin Cruise</h3><p>Calm seas in NovemberDuration: 2hrs</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/sandbank-trip-in-maldives.webp" alt="Sandbank Excursion" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Sandbank Excursion</h3><p>Perfect weather in NovemberDuration: 3-4hrs</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/fishing/night-fishing-in-maldives.webp" alt="Sunset Fishing" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Sunset Fishing</h3><p>Excellent catches in NovemberDuration: 2-3hrs</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/island-hopping3.webp" alt="Island Hopping" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Island Hopping</h3><p>Reliable transfers in NovemberDuration: Full day</p><h2>Is November a Good Time to Visit the Maldives?</h2><p>November offers an excellent balance of favorable weather conditions and pre-peak season value in the Maldives. As the northeast monsoon (Iruvai) establishes, rainfall decreases significantly, humidity levels drop, and sunshine hours increase, creating near-ideal conditions for a tropical vacation. While not quite as consistently perfect as the peak dry season months (December-March), November provides substantially better weather than the wet season months at a more attractive price point.</p><p>November is an excellent time to visit the Maldives if:</p><ul><li>You''re seeking excellent weather conditions without paying peak season prices</li><li>You value underwater visibility for snorkeling and diving experiences</li><li>You prefer moderate tourist numbers rather than peak season crowds</li><li>You''re interested in marine life encounters with excellent visibility conditions</li><li>You want reliable transfer conditions with fewer weather-related delays</li><li>You''re interested in experiencing Republic Day celebrations on November 11th</li><li>You prefer lower humidity and more comfortable temperatures</li><li>You want to secure reservations at popular resorts before the peak season rush</li><li>You enjoy water sports in calm sea conditions</li></ul><p>November may not be ideal if:</p><ul><li>You''re seeking the absolute lowest prices possible (July-September offers deeper discounts)</li><li>You require absolutely guaranteed perfect weather every day (January-February would be better)</li><li>You''re specifically interested in surfing, as swells decrease with the northeast monsoon</li><li>You''re visiting very early in November and have a very short stay, as the transition from wet season is still in progress</li><li>You''re looking for the most vibrant resort atmosphere with maximum occupancy (peak season offers more)</li></ul><p>For most travelers, November represents an excellent compromise between weather quality and value. The improving conditions, decreasing rainfall, and increasing sunshine hours combined with pre-peak season pricing make it one of the best &quot;value months&quot; in the Maldives calendar. The gradually increasing tourist numbers also mean that resorts are more lively than during the wet season months, but still far from the crowded conditions of the peak season.</p><p>If you''re considering a November visit to the Maldives, it''s worth comparing with other months to find the perfect timing for your preferences. Check our guides on visiting in October and visiting in December to compare conditions across different periods of the year.</p><p>For comprehensive information about the best times to visit throughout the year, see our complete guide on the cheapest time to visit the Maldives, which provides a month-by-month breakdown of weather, prices, and crowd levels.</p>', 13 from nodes where node_type = 'article' and slug = 'maldives-in-november-weather-activities-expert-travel-guide' on conflict (id) do update set body = excluded.body, reading_time_minutes = excluded.reading_time_minutes;
